# Patch / install Architect Library (global default)

When the user asks to **install library**, **install the library**, **patch library**, **refresh library**, **update library**, **install skills and agents**, **sync library**, **update architect library** — or **patch**, **upgrade**, **install**, or **refresh** skills or agents — or you finish adding/changing `skills/` or `agents/` in this repo — **run the full library install yourself** (`bash scripts/install_library.sh` with no args) — do not only edit source folders.

Use partial installs (`skills` or `agents` only) **only** when the user explicitly asks.

**Source of truth:**

- Skills: `<repo>/skills/<name>/`
- Agents: `<repo>/agents/<name>/` (assembled to a single `.md` at install)

**Global install targets (default):**

| Library | Cursor | Copilot |
|---------|--------|---------|
| Skills | `~/.cursor/skills/<name>/` | `~/.copilot/skills/<name>/` |
| Agents | `~/.cursor/agents/<name>.md` | `~/.copilot/agents/<name>.agent.md` |

Use **per-project** `.cursor/skills/` / `.github/skills/` only if the user explicitly wants project-local install (`install_library.sh … project`).

Do **not** copy skills into `<repo>/.cursor/skills/` or agents into `<repo>/.cursor/agents/` — that duplicates source and breaks the install model.

## Bundles (in `scripts/install_library.sh`)

```
SKILL_BUNDLE="excalidraw-diagram word-document powerpoint-presentation spreadsheet-document pdf-document _shared"
AGENT_BUNDLE="code-review"
```

- **New** skill or agent → add to bundle and install target.
- **Existing** entry → **replace** whole folder/file (`rm -rf` then fresh copy/assemble).

## Patch procedure (global default)

From the repository root:

```bash
REPO=/path/to/architect-library
cd "$REPO"
bash scripts/install_library.sh
```

Partial installs:

```bash
bash scripts/install_library.sh skills
bash scripts/install_library.sh agents
bash scripts/install_library.sh all cursor
bash scripts/install_library.sh all copilot
```

## Verify

```bash
test -f ~/.cursor/skills/_shared/office-tools/office_tools.py
test -f ~/.cursor/skills/word-document/SKILL.md
test -f ~/.cursor/agents/code-review.md
test -f ~/.copilot/agents/code-review.agent.md
grep -q 'readonly: true' ~/.cursor/agents/code-review.md
```

The install script runs these checks automatically.

## After patching

1. Tell the user skills and agents were updated under `~/.cursor/` and `~/.copilot/`.
2. Ask them to **open a new agent chat** (or reload the window) so skill descriptions and agents reload.
3. Runtimes are separate: run `bash scripts/install_deps.sh` from the **repo clone**, not from installed skill folders.

Full paths, Copilot/Claude variants, and mistakes to avoid: [docs/AGENT-SKILL-INSTALL.md](docs/AGENT-SKILL-INSTALL.md).
